% ---------------------------------------------------------
% FONT -- chosen for ATS text extraction, not just looks.
%
% Arial is the safest resume font for parsers. Carlito is the
% metric-compatible Calibri clone and is always present on Overleaf.
% TeX Gyre Heros (a Helvetica clone) ships with every TeX Live, so the
% chain always terminates in something that exists and never errors.
%
% Ligatures=NoCommon is the ATS-relevant part: it stops "fi"/"fl" from
% being merged into single glyphs, which some parsers extract as
% mojibake or drop entirely.
% ---------------------------------------------------------
\defaultfontfeatures{Ligatures=NoCommon}

% TeX Gyre Heros is the free Helvetica/Arial clone. It ships with every TeX
% Live and Overleaf install, so it needs no conditional, and Helvetica/Arial
% letterforms are the most conventional shape an ATS or recruiter will see.
%
% Chosen over Carlito for x-height. Carlito (Calibri metrics) has an x-height
% of 0.478em against Verdana's 0.545em, so it renders ~12% smaller at the same
% point size -- the text looked shrunken. Heros is 0.523em, which restores
% almost all of the apparent size at the same nominal sizes.
%
% Do NOT reintroduce \IfFontExistsTF{Arial}/{Verdana} here. fontconfig aliases
% those names to substitutes, so the test returns TRUE and then \setmainfont
% fails on the missing file -- the chain never falls through, it just errors.
% That is what the original Verdana block did.
\setmainfont{TeX Gyre Heros}[Ligatures=NoCommon]
% \setmainfont{Arial}[Ligatures=NoCommon]     % only where Arial is genuinely installed
% \setmainfont{Carlito}[Ligatures=NoCommon]   % Calibri metrics; smaller on the page

% General document typography
